---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const downloadLink = "/downloads/RobloxAccountManager-Setup.exe";

const docsSections = [
  {
    id: "getting-started",
    title: "1. Getting Started & Windows Setup",
    content: `
      Roblox Account Manager is packaged as a standalone 64-bit Windows desktop executable. No prerequisite runtimes or Python environments are needed.
      
      Requirements:
      • Windows 10 (Build 19041+) or Windows 11 64-bit
      • Standard Roblox Player installed from the official Roblox website
      • Administrative permissions only if installing to C:\\Program Files (portable mode recommended)
    `
  },
  {
    id: "account-vault",
    title: "2. Encrypted Vault & Cookie Management",
    content: `
      Your account credentials and .ROBLOSECURITY cookies are kept securely in an encrypted local database using AES-256 GCM.
      
      How to Import an Account:
      1. Open Roblox Account Manager and navigate to the "Accounts" tab on the sidebar.
      2. Click "+ Import Cookie" or "Add Account".
      3. Enter your account username and paste your .ROBLOSECURITY cookie token.
      4. The Account Checker immediately validates the token against the official Roblox API and displays the account's age, Robux balance, and avatar thumbnail.
      5. Your token is encrypted with your master vault key and saved to your local drive.
    `
  },
  {
    id: "multi-instance",
    title: "3. Multi-Instance Launching Workflow",
    content: `
      Roblox Account Manager leverages native Windows mutex bypass hooks so you can run two or more concurrent Roblox client processes on the same computer.
      
      Launching Multiple Accounts:
      1. Open the "Launch" tab on the left sidebar.
      2. Check or select the accounts you wish to launch from your vaulted list.
      3. Choose your destination mode:
         • Game (Place ID or Experience URL)
         • Private Server (VIP server link or code)
         • Job ID (Specific server instance ID)
         • Join Person (Username to follow into game)
      4. Adjust the "Wait between accounts" slider (recommended 5s - 10s to ensure clean game client initializations).
      5. Click the primary "Launch" button. Each client will spawn in sequence.
    `
  },
  {
    id: "fps-optimization",
    title: "4. FPS Uncapping & Background Throttling",
    content: `
      By default, the standard Roblox client locks render framerate to 60 FPS. Roblox Account Manager allows you to unlock framerates or optimize resource usage:
      
      • Unlocked FPS: Set to 144, 240, or Unlimited for ultra-smooth gameplay on high-refresh-rate monitors.
      • Background Throttling: Automatically lowers background client windows to 15 or 30 FPS. This saves immense GPU power, VRAM, and CPU utilization when running 5+ instances simultaneously.
    `
  },
  {
    id: "webhooks",
    title: "5. Discord Webhooks & Event Notifications",
    content: `
      You can configure Roblox Account Manager to send real-time alerts directly to a channel in your Discord server:
      
      1. Go to "Settings" -> "Webhooks" in the desktop app.
      2. Paste your Discord Webhook URL.
      3. Toggle the events you want to monitor:
         • Launch Successful
         • Disconnect / Game Crash Watchdog
         • Daily Account Balance & RAP Summary
      4. Hit "Send Test Webhook" to verify communication.
    `
  },
  {
    id: "troubleshooting",
    title: "6. Troubleshooting & Common Questions",
    content: `
      • "Windows protected your PC" (SmartScreen): Because this is a fresh testing build, Windows SmartScreen may show an unknown publisher warning. Click "More info" and select "Run anyway".
      • Game crashes on second launch: Ensure "Multi-Instance" is enabled in Settings and set a longer delay (e.g. 8-10 seconds) between launches on slower machines.
      • Cookie expired notice: If you log out manually from a web browser, Roblox invalidates that session token. Re-extract your fresh .ROBLOSECURITY cookie and update the account in your vault.
    `
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Documentation" description="Complete user guide for Roblox Account Manager: installation on Windows, importing accounts, multi-instance configuration, and troubleshooting.">
  
  <div class="py-16 sm:py-24 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16 reveal-on-scroll">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-300 border border-purple-500/20 mb-4">
        User Manual & Reference
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6">
        Roblox Account Manager <span class="gradient-text">Documentation</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Everything you need to know about setting up, launching, and managing accounts with Roblox Account Manager on Windows.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Docs Layout: Sidebar index + Content body -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
      
      <!-- Table of Contents sticky sidebar -->
      <aside class="hidden lg:block lg:col-span-4 sticky top-28 glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
          On This Page
        </h2>
        <nav class="space-y-2 text-sm">
          {docsSections.map((sec) => (
            <a 
              href={`#${sec.id}`} 
              class="block py-1.5 px-2.5 rounded-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-purple-600 dark:hover:text-purple-400 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors text-xs font-medium"
            >
              {sec.title}
            </a>
          ))}
        </nav>
        
        <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10">
          <a 
            href={downloadLink}
            download="RobloxAccountManager-Setup.exe"
            class="w-full flex items-center justify-center gap-2 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-bold text-xs text-white bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-blue-600 shadow-md hover:scale-105 transition-all text-center"
          >
            <span>Download .exe Installer</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Main Docs Content Area -->
      <main class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-8">
        {docsSections.map((sec) => (
          <section id={sec.id} class="glass-panel rounded-3xl p-8 sm:p-10 reveal-on-scroll scroll-mt-28">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-purple-500"></span>
              {sec.title}
            </h2>
            <div class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line font-sans space-y-3">
              {sec.content.trim()}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))}
      </main>

    </div>

  </div>

</Layout>

